  "articleBody": "Remodeling your bathroom can feel like a big undertaking, and a common question we get is, \"How long will this really take?\" It's a fair question, and the honest answer is: it varies! Lead times for materials are often the biggest factor here. Some products, like custom vanities or specialty tiles, can take up to 8 weeks to arrive. This means that even before we swing a hammer, there's a good chunk of planning and waiting involved. Then, once everything is on-site, the actual construction phase can range from a few weeks to several months, depending on how extensive the changes are. Are we just swapping out a tub for a shower, or are we reconfiguring the entire layout? The more custom work involved, the longer the project will naturally take. That's why having a clear vision and discussing product lead times early on is so crucial. We'll help you map out a realistic timeline, keeping you informed every step of the way, because open communication is a big deal to us at HH Remodeling LLC. We're here to make sure you know what to expect and when.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}